{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.EwSlotFarCommutationObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.EwSlotFarCommutationObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Submonoid.Centralizer"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.su2L_generator_escapes_slots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.su2L_generator_escapes_slots","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L237-L247","doc":"**Equivalent positive form.** Given the non-abelian `su(2)_L` structure\nrelation `⁅J₁, J₂⁆ = J₃ ≠ 0`, at least one of the two adjoint generators is\n**not** in the slot subalgebra: the non-abelian pair cannot both be slot-built.\nThe escape is the inter-slot linking. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.su2L_nonabelianness_not_in_slots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.su2L_nonabelianness_not_in_slots","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L216-L235","doc":"**The far-commutation obstruction (capstone).** Suppose two `su(2)_L` adjoint\ngenerators `J₁, J₂` obey the structure relation `⁅J₁, J₂⁆ = J₃` with `J₃ ≠ 0`\n(the gauge algebra is genuinely non-abelian), and suppose *both* are realised\ninside the slot subalgebra generated by the far-commuting slots `σ₁, σ₃, σ₅`.\nThis is **impossible**.\n\nThe proof: the slot subalgebra is mutually abelian\n(`slotSubmonoid_commutative`), so `J₁` and `J₂` commute; but a nonzero bracket\nforbids commutation (`nonabelian_bracket_forbids_commute`). Hence the non-abelian\n`su(2)_L` structure **cannot** be carried purely among the far-commuting slots —\nit must arise from the inter-slot linking (`σ₂, σ₄` / `Lk_R`,\n`interSlot_not_farApart`). A genuine structural exclusion, not a numerical\nnear-miss. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction","label":"prop:ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.carriers_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.carriers_commute","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L195-L206","doc":"**The EW carriers pairwise commute** (abelian) — `W·Z = Z·W`, `W·H = H·W`,\n`Z·H = H·Z` for `W = σ₁⁴, Z = σ₃⁶, H = σ₅⁸`. The disjoint-pair construction is\nan *abelian* subalgebra; this is the positive, non-vacuous content grounding the\nobstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.carriers_mem_slotSubmonoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.carriers_mem_slotSubmonoid","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L183-L193","doc":"The actual EW carriers `W ↔ σ₁⁴`, `Z ↔ σ₃⁶`, `H ↔ σ₅⁸` are members of the\nslot submonoid (powers of the generators). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.slotSubmonoid_commutative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.slotSubmonoid_commutative","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L175-L181","doc":"**The slot subalgebra is mutually abelian.** Any two elements of the slot\nsubmonoid commute — the concrete \"far-commuting slots generate a commutative\nsubalgebra\" claim, sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.slot_generators_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.slot_generators_commute","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L156-L173","doc":"The three slot generators pairwise commute (from far-commutation +\n`slot_indices_farApart`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.slotSubmonoid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.slotSubmonoid","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L151-L154","doc":"The submonoid generated by the three slot generators `σ₁, σ₃, σ₅` — the\n\"slot subalgebra\" that hosts the EW carriers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.BraidGenerators.farCommute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.BraidGenerators.farCommute","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L149-L149","doc":"Far-commutation: generators with indices `≥ 2` apart commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.BraidGenerators.gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.BraidGenerators.gen","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L147-L147","doc":"The generator `σ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.BraidGenerators.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.BraidGenerators.mk","kind":"ctor","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L145-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.BraidGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.BraidGenerators","kind":"structure","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L142-L149","doc":"Braid generators in a monoid `A`, carrying the **far-commutation relation**\n`σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` for `|i − j| ≥ 2` as its defining field (a presentation\nrelation of the braid group `B_n` and its Hecke quotient `H_n(q)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.interSlot_not_farApart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.interSlot_not_farApart","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L132-L138","doc":"The adjacent (inter-slot) generators `σ₂, σ₄` are **not** far apart from the\nslots they bridge: `|2−1| = |2−3| = |4−3| = |4−5| = 1 < 2`. These are precisely\nthe generators the braid far-commutation relation does *not* cover — the seat of\nthe non-abelian structure (the categorical linking `Lk_R` acts here). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.slot_indices_farApart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.slot_indices_farApart","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L126-L130","doc":"The three slot indices are pairwise far apart (`|1−3| = 2`, `|1−5| = 4`,\n`|3−5| = 2`), a decidable combinatorial fact about the positions `1, 3, 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.farApart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.farApart","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L120-L124","doc":"Two braid-generator indices are **far apart** when they differ by at least\n`2` — exactly the regime `|i − j| ≥ 2` of the braid far-commutation relation\n`σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i`. (Over `ℕ` the truncated subtraction makes this the honest\nsymmetric gap condition.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.commute_of_mem_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.commute_of_mem_closure","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L78-L108","doc":"**The submonoid generated by a pairwise-commuting set is commutative.** Any\ntwo elements of `Submonoid.closure S` commute, provided every pair drawn from `S`\ncommutes. Proved through the centralizer submonoid (`closure S ≤ centralizer S`,\nthen `closure S ≤ centralizer ↑(closure S)`), no induction bookkeeping. This is\nthe \"the whole slot subalgebra is abelian, not just the generators\" statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.nonabelian_bracket_forbids_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.nonabelian_bracket_forbids_commute","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L63-L70","doc":"**A nonzero bracket forbids commutation (the crux).** If the `su(2)_L`\nstructure relation `⁅x, y⁆ = z` holds with `z ≠ 0` (a genuinely non-abelian\nbracket), then `x` and `y` do **not** commute. Contrapositive: commuting\ngenerators cannot realise a nonzero adjoint bracket. Not vacuous — it runs\n`bracket_eq_zero_of_commute` against `z ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.bracket_eq_zero_of_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.bracket_eq_zero_of_commute","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L57-L61","doc":"**Commuting operators have zero bracket.** The defining fact of the\nobstruction: on a commutative subalgebra every commutator vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.bracket","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/ew-slot-far-commutation-obstruction.lean#L53-L55","doc":"The ring commutator `⁅x, y⁆ = x·y − y·x`. Its vanishing is the algebraic\ncontent of \"`x` and `y` commute\". ","signatureChunk":0}]}